   "subject": "Re: Over-time Actor-partner Interdependence Model (correlations)",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"font-family:&quot;trebuchet ms&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(51,51,51)\">If I understand correctly, Lavaan treats Time1 for both subjects as an exogenous variable and gives their covariance.</div></div></blockquote><div><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Yes, if you use the<font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> sem() </font>or<span style=\"font-family:&quot;courier new&quot;,monospace\"> </span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;courier new&quot;,monospace\">cfa()</span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;courier new&quot;,monospace\"> </span>functions, exogenous covariances are estimated by default.</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"font-family:&quot;trebuchet ms&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(51,51,51)\">I would like to ask if there is any possibility to estimate correlations within Time2 and within Time3 or maybe I choose the wrong method.</div></div></blockquote><div><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>The residual covariances controlling for autoregressive effect of a previous occasion, whereas the exogenous covariance does not.  You can request them in correlation metric (the<font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> std.all </font>column) with<font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> summary(..., std = TRUE)</font>.</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"font-size:small\"><div style=\"font-size:13px\">Terrence D. Jorgensen</div><div style=\"font-size:13px\">Postdoctoral Researcher, Methods and Statistics</div><div style=\"font-size:13px\">Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam</div><div style=\"font-size:13px\">UvA web page: <a href=\"http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen\" style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792425256901000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0iMcNRE_2V0hj06Succr6r\">http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen</a></div><div><br></div></div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
